WEBVTT

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:16.160
I'm not like the others. I don't think
you're perfect or anything like that.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.950
So, remember: This is normal.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.330
That's why, I would like to serve on the student council!

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.000
Good morning, Touko.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.080
G'morning!

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.950
Good morning!

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.830
Sayaka.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:14.870
Touko!

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:15.830
Good morning.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.790
'Morning. You seem in high spirits.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.830
Oh! There's the presidential couple.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.500
Who are you calling a "couple"?

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.450
Morning.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.040
Which one's the husband?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.250
It's gotta be Nanami, right?

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.540
So, are you planning to announce it today?

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:31.750
Yep.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.250
It's about time.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.250
I can finally get started. Will you help me?

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.620
Of course I will, if that's what you want.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.580
MATH 1

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.620
Koyomi! Can I erase the blackboard now?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.950
Huh? Uh...

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.540
Yeah, sure.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.000
Sorry, I wasn't actually looking at the blackboard!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.660
What? Seriously?

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.700
Then what've you been writing so furiously over here?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.370
N-nothing really.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.250
Okay then. See you tomorrow.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.950
Akari seems pretty happy today.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.870
Yeah.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.200
Koito-san!

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.000
Look, it's the student council president.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.450
Koito sure is connected.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.750
Usually people go meet the President,
not the other way around.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.750
I wanted to see you as soon as possible.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.250
Senpai.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.160
Um...

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.250
What?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.750
You're too close.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.660
A-am I?

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.410
Can't you tell?

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.250
Your idea of personal space is totally not normal.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.870
It could cause problems if people start
misinterpreting our relationship, right?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.660
I mean, everyone admires you in
one way or another, Nanami-senpai.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.750
I don't think there's any room for misinterpretation.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.160
Of course, there is!

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:57.620
Okay, fine.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.000
I'll be more careful.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.250
Oh, you're early.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.370
Hey. What's up?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.200
Who's this?

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.120
Dojima-kun. He's a first-year.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.080
Yup! Nice to meetcha!

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.450
Kuze-senpai introduced him to me.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.410
Kuze-senpai was in the same club as me in junior high.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.000
You mean the kendo club? So, you aren't
going to join the one we have here?

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.950
Nah. I was pretty weak, so I figured
I'd try something new in high school.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.750
Besides, I hear being on the student council
scores us bonus points on our report cards.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.080
I'm Yuu Koito, a first-year like you.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:33.620
Cool.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.250
You're the one who did that campaign speech, right?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.370
Will this kid actually be helpful to us?

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.620
Well, Senpai is the one who recommended him,
so I think he'll do fine.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.660
Ah, yes.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.290
That's exactly why I'm worried.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.370
Man, having capable subordinates
sure makes things easy!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.830
But it's precisely because Senpai has that personality
that he's good at finding talented people.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.160
I guess that's one way to look at it.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:57.660
In the end, Dojima-kun came here of his own will.
So that's a good sign, right?

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.080
Now that everyone is here, I'll introduce myself again...

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.040
I'm Touko Nanami, the Student Council President.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.450
And I'm the Vice-President, Sayaka Saeki.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:10.700
For the time being, the Student Council will be
managed by the five members here.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.830
Please do your best over the next year.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.200
Midterm Tests
Sports Day
End of Semester Exams
Summer Vacation
Cultural Festival!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.250
Aside from our daily duties, these school events will
be the hardest to deal with, so prepare yourself.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.500
And the biggest of this year's events is going to be...

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.080
Let's hear it, Koito-san!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.450
Huh? U-um... the Cultural Festival?

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.700
That's right. The Cultural Festival!

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:34.660
Our responsibility is to work behind-the-scenes to
ensure all students can fully enjoy the event.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.870
Mainly, we will be adjusting locations and schedules,
in addition to giving orders to sub-committees.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.290
Sounds pretty dull.

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:41.910
It's an important job.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.830
But that's not all.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.830
Along with working behind-the-scenes,
there's something else I'd like to do...

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.080
Bring back the Student Council Stage Show!

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.160
Bring back... the stage show?

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.830
A stage show is the norm at Cultural Festivals, but...

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.580
the Student Council will do one, too?

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.910
Our school doesn't have a Theater Club, right?

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:10.620
Art Room

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:13.870
So, in the past, other clubs like the Art club and the
Woodworking club all planned a stage show together.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:17.290
There's a lot of work to be done to make
a good stage show, like costume and set design.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:20.160
That's why they figured they could use
their individual skills to make it happen.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:23.870
But even so, they just couldn't find enough actors.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.040
And that's where... the Student Council came in?

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.160
The members of the Student Council must've been
really enthusiastic back then.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.200
After that, it became annual tradition.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.410
But, um... I think it was seven years ago...

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.450
it looks like the tradition just stopped.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.500
I thought it might be fun to revive that tradition. Well?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.330
Sounds fun. I want in!

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.160
Really?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.200
Hm, to be honest, I'm not sure...

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.250
Our responsibilities keep us busy enough already.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.080
I wasn't under the impression that joining
the Student Council would mean doing a stage show!

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.290
I see...

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:05.160
Well, it's just an idea for now. We have some time
until the Cultural Festival, so think it over.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.200
With that said, let's put aside the decision of
whether to do the stage show

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.200
and focus on the more important part
of planning the festival, which is...

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.950
Sorting documents?

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.200
We're inheriting this job from the previous cabinet...

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.580
so, we'd like to sort these documents
into categorized files.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:29.700
All the budget and operation reports will be put in
the Student Council room, so keep those separate.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:34.370
Good work.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:37.950
Say, Koito-san, did you totally want to join
the Student Council or something?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.700
I wouldn't go that far... Why?

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:44.660
Well, you ended your campaign speech by talking
about how you were going to join the council.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.620
I thought, "Man, she's really pumped up."

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.410
No, I just got caught up in the moment, so to speak...

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:55.750
It was more like, I started out just by lending a hand,
then went with the flow and ended up here.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.250
How 'bout you?

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.540
I joined because I was a member of
the Student Council in junior high.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.450
Back in elementary school,
I participated in some sport clubs,

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:11.080
but I found that I'm more suited to support roles
rather than putting in the effort to stand out.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.660
So, you want to be the manager?

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.000
That could definitely be a trait
of someone fit for the student council.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.370
That's why I'm not sure I could handle a stage show, too.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.500
If it's something behind-the-scenes,
though, I'd gladly do it.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.290
Say, isn't this...

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.870
Mystery Club's
Murder Investigation

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.910
one of the old scripts?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.410
Yeah. It looks it got mixed in with those other documents.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:41.870
There were other copies left in the Student Council room,
which is how Touko got the idea of reviving it.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:49.540
If it was really such a tradition,
I wonder why it stopped seven years ago...

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:53.540
Senpai?

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.500
We're supposed to be working right now.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.410
You're right. Of course.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:10.040
It finally feels like we've made some progress...

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:16.120
Oh, it's late! I have to get going soon.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.040
Ah! You have the Flower Club today, right?

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.410
Yeah. Sorry.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.700
No worries. Thanks for staying as long as you could.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.750
That's enough work for today, everyone.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.750
I still need to use the computer for some work, so I'll stay.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.910
Good work y'all.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.040
Okay, I'll be excusing myself for today.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.540
Me too, I guess.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.790
Excuse... me...

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:44.700
Maybe I'll use the computer for a little while, too.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.540
What are you doing? Homework?

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.580
You can use it, Koito-san.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.580
I've got my own at home anyway.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.500
I don't really need to use it, either.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.410
You know, you really...

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.000
Just go with the flow, right?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.370
I already know.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.450
No...

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:19.700
You're kind.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.290
Hey, Yuu.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.000
I'd like to kiss you.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:40.580
Although you said it's okay if I don't love you back,
I see you're still coming on to me.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.700
W-well, I didn't want to take you
by surprise like last time, so-!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:45.950
That's a poor excuse!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:52.000
Do you really think it's acceptable for the
Student Council President to be so fickle with her words?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.250
I mean...

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.250
I just can't help it!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.410
You're always willing to tolerate my feelings, and it...

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:07.160
it just makes me want you more.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.200
It's all because of Yuu.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.200
I'm jealous.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.660
I wish I could be like that.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.200
Huh?

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.330
Never mind, it's nothing.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.370
Okay.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.950
If you want to... that's fine.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.580
Really?! Why?

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:46.410
It's not as if I hate it or anything.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.660
And if I said I wasn't interested, well...

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.120
I'd be lying.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.000
What does that mean?

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.370
You want to kiss even though you don't even like me?

00:11:58.950 --> 00:11:59.870
Yuu...

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.500
You perv.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.830
If you're going to make fun of me, then I'm leaving!

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.540
Wait! Don't be hasty!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.830
Let's kiss.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.000
She has long eyelashes.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.750
Someone forgot their pencil case.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.450
Maybe it was Maki-kun...

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.950
The Distance Between Fondness and Kisses

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:06.000
Not One of the Characters

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:27.750
This is yours, isn't it? I found it in
the Student Council Room yesterday.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.620
Ah, is that where I left it?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.870
Yup. Here.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.160
Thanks.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:34.910
Hey...

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:35.580
What?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.040
What were you doing yesterday?

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.080
What do you mean?

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.750
You stayed behind with Nanami-senpai, right?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.950
I was just wondering what you two
were doing on the computer.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:49.120
O-oh, um...

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:54.750
Just looking up info on classes, homework,
and what will be on the mid-terms. And stuff.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.410
Whoa, that's great. I'd like to learn that, too.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.450
Oh! I have to get going.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.500
Thanks. See you after school.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.410
Yeah.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:10.950
I nearly panicked. Just stay calm, stay calm...

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.660
Well, just sit down and have some tea.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.120
There are plenty of snacks, too.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:23.160
You can bribe me all you want,
but I won't agree to that stage show.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.830
Here, here, here.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.080
I can't bait you into this either, huh?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:33.330
You don't give up, huh? I figured you were
the type who gives under pressure.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.830
Even a small role is fine.
Once you get into it I swear it'll be fun.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.120
I hate being in front of crowds.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.040
Do neither of you have trouble with that?

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:47.540
I don't struggle with it.
You don't have any problems either, right?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.790
Well, no. I wouldn't even mind being the leading actress.

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.080
What is she talking about?

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.700
During your election speech,
you managed to keep up the perfect front,

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:04.870
but on the inside, you were a nervous wreck.
But now you want to do a stage show?

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:10.160
You may be good at "acting" I guess, but still...

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.080
Why are you so determined to do this stage show?

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:16.750
I only have this one chance to participate
in the Cultural Festival as President.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:19.660
So, why wouldn't I want to make things interesting?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.750
Can't that be reason enough?

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.910
Come on, let's do it!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.450
No way!

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:28.410
But, why?

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:32.620
I just told you why! I hate being in front of crowds.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.700
You just have to pretend you're NOT in front of a crowd.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.580
Maki.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.540
Yo, Maki!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.830
I can't do that.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.200
Yes, you can.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.200
Yeah?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.200
What're you grinning about?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.950
The only way to know if I can do it or not is if I actually do it!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.950
Is that how I looked just now?

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.290
You totally did.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.290
Right. That's why you should try!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:46.410
Still, we lucked out having two beautiful bombshells
in our student council, huh?

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.040
You can't trick me into this.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.120
Let's just try!

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.700
No thank you.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.580
Uh... Sure.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:51.750
Why don't we put a pin in that idea and come back to it
once we've thought things over?

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.370
So, are you into Nanami?

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.120
Or are you Team Saeki?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:52.750
Should we?

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.620
Ah! Maybe, of all people, you like Koito-san?

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.160
No, no...

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:01.200
Just tell me already. Which one is your type?

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:07.330
I don't know what to say...
I don't really have a certain "type."

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.790
Could one of you help me take these files
over to the Reference Room?

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.540
Ah, I'll do it.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:18.200
Reference Room

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.950
Maki-kun, are you opposed to the stage show, too?

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.500
If we don't have to do it, then I'd certainly prefer not to.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.040
I see...

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.790
Well, this isn't an official Student Council duty
so we can't force you into it...

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.660
If two of our first-year members are against it,
we should rethink the whole thing, huh?

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:35.830
I'm not as firmly opposed to it as Koito-san is, though.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:39.450
Touko has tried so hard to convince her, and yet...

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.450
Nanami-senpai has really taken
a liking to Koito-san, hasn't she?

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:55.040
They hadn't even met until recently, is that right?

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:58.830
Yes. And I can't figure out what
about that girl she likes so much.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:03.700
Koito-san is really nice!
She worked so hard on that campaign speech.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:04.790
Yeah, sure...

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:09.750
Are you maybe holding a grudge because
you didn't get asked to give that speech instead?

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.040
Does it seem that way?

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:17.330
Well, I think Touko's just excited
to finally be a real senpai to someone.

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.290
She'll comes to her senses soon.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.290
Maki-kun, are you heading to the staff room?

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:29.450
Ah, yeah. I have to deliver this.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.200
I need to get some copies done, so let's go together.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.500
Thank you very much!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.950
Let's make sure that stage show doesn't happen.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.750
You really hate the idea, huh?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.330
Yup.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:47.250
Still, I wonder if they've already talked
to the other clubs about it...

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:51.080
The way they were acting,
I think they've already started pre-prep.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.450
They're getting too caught up in it!

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.160
Whatever Nanami-senpai says, people do, huh?

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.290
You sure know a lot about Senpai.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.080
Huh?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:06.750
Well, I think we get along pretty well.
It's already been a month or so since we've met.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.120
Koito-san, are you dating Nanami-senpai?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.000
I saw you two yesterday. Sorry.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.750
He saw us...

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.580
He knows!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.790
If he tells anyone else...

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.330
Is Nanami-senpai seriously dating a first-year girl?

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.910
This whole time, she was saying how she
"didn't intend to go out with anyone"!

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.450
So that's how it was, Touko.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.910
You let her give your campaign speech
because she was your girlfriend?

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.370
Koito-san.

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:59.290
It's okay. Just because I saw doesn't mean I'll-

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:00.330
Maki-kun.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:06.080
Don't tell Nanami-senpai what you saw.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:10.410
If that's what you want, then, okay. But why?

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:15.870
Senpai is... Well, she's busy and has
a lot of things to think about right now.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:20.160
I don't want her to get hurt by something
she doesn't need to know about.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:22.160
Please!

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:28.830
She's the first thing that
you're worried about, huh? Interesting.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.750
People in love sure are fascinating!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:43.080
I was raised in a family with two older sisters
and one younger, which is probably why

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.450
I often find myself the guy that
girls confide their problems to.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:53.200
Actually, we really hit it off, so I was wondering
if I should ask for a phone number or something...

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.580
Still, that doesn't bother me.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.660
Girls tend to enjoy talking about love.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:00.290
That's how I find myself following
so many real-life romance stories.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:03.450
Maki-kun!

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:09.250
Um, well, you're such a good listener that suddenly
I've found myself thinking more about you and...

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.660
The heck is that?

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:16.250
A character from the story shouldn't fall
in love with a spectator. It's disappointing.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.910
I don't want anything like that.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.410
I just want to sit in the stands and
watch the story unfold upon the stage.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.620
I've found it...

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.790
A new love story!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.700
It's a secret performance only I know about.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.950
I want to watch it up close... in my special, reserved seat!

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.580
I have to watch close, and with care.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:57.040
Don't worry. I won't say anything to Senpai.
I won't mention it to anyone else, either.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:58.750
I promise.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:09.410
Okay. I trust you. I mean, you came right out
and told me that you saw us.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:13.080
From now on, you should be a little more careful, okay?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.660
Yeah...

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:20.660
Still! We're not actually dating or anything!

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.950
There you go, making excuses again.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:23.540
I'm telling you, you've got it wrong!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.120
I have to admit, I was a little surprised.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:30.620
When I was there, it looked like Nanami-senpai's
feelings toward you were pretty one-sided.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.250
But, Koito-san...

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.660
Now I can tell that you like Nanami-senpai as well.

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:39.790
Huh?

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:45.290
I mean, you've been more worried
about her than you. And that means...

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:48.790
Nanami-senpai must mean something special to you.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:52.120
I like her?

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.700
But I...

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:57.910
I didn't think you were the type to get flustered!

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:00.790
No way...

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.870
I mean, this is just...

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:10.200
it's just normal, after all.
